<title>UK: DCS shares rise on Swiss contract award.</title>
<headline>DCS shares rise on Swiss contract award.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in computer services group DCS Group Plc shot higher on Monday, after the company announced a major contract with Swiss freight group Kuehne &amp; Nagel Group AG.</p>
<p>DCS said the contract allowed Kuehne &amp; Nagel unlimited worldwide use of DCS's logistics software package CIEL/400 to support its global forwarding and logistics services.</p>
<p>Kuehne &amp; Nagel chairman and chief executive said: &quot;With CIEL/400 we are looking forward to significantly strengthening our information systems worldwide.&quot;</p>
<p>DCS shares were up 27p at 319-1/2 by 1600 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
